WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:05.520
The live-action adaptation of "The Little&nbsp;
Mermaid" has arrived and early reactions to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:10.510
the film are largely positive. So why should&nbsp;
moviegoers want to be a part of its world?

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:14.400
Those who attended the premiere cite&nbsp;
the captivating performances and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:20.220
infectious musical numbers, led by Halle&nbsp;
Bailey as Ariel. Several lucky fans took&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:24.480
to Twitter to share their thoughts,&nbsp;
including an R &amp; B icon who knows a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:27.646
thing or two about making waves&nbsp;
with a powerful musical number.

00:00:27.646 --> 00:00:33.840
Naturally, after a series of divisive live-action&nbsp;
Disney remakes, viewers are a bit apprehensive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:39.060
about the upcoming release, particularly&nbsp;
about the too-realistic designs of beloved&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:44.520
characters like Flounder and Sebastian. But a&nbsp;
sample of early reactions should assure fans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:49.006
that “The Little Mermaid” offers a faithful&nbsp;
adaptation of the classic animated film.

00:00:49.006 --> 00:00:54.720
Strong performances in the 2023 version&nbsp;
reportedly drive the film and make it more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.720 --> 00:01:00.600
lively than other Disney live-action adaptations.&nbsp;
Viewers fortunate enough to catch the film early&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:07.020
single out Melissa McCarthy's portrayal of&nbsp;
the devious sea witch Ursula and Daveed Diggs'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:12.335
lively singing as Sebastian, in addition&nbsp;
to Bailey's impressive depiction of Ariel.

00:01:12.685 --> 00:01:16.401
"I've been watching you for a long time, dearie."

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:20.110
When Things Go Pop writer&nbsp;
Brandon Lewis wrote on Twitter,

00:01:20.110 --> 00:01:26.220
"I was blown away by ["The Little Mermaid"]. Some&nbsp;
visual issues aside, it's the most romantic and,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:32.700
dare I say, magical Disney has been in years.&nbsp;
The best live-action remake by a mile. Daveed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:38.760
Diggs is the MVP. Halle Bailey is a superstar,&nbsp;
and her 'Part of Your World' is a showstopper."

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:43.260
In addition to the heartfelt performances,&nbsp;
many are looking forward to the show-stopping&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:48.720
musical numbers that made the original film&nbsp;
such a cherished Disney classic. So far,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:52.500
many early reactions claim that&nbsp;
"The Little Mermaid" lives up to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:57.357
expectations and accurately recreates&nbsp;
what made the original so special.

00:01:57.357 --> 00:02:00.300
Meanwhile, Discussing Film writer A. Felicia&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:04.740
Wade still loved the film despite&nbsp;
some slight criticisms, posting,

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:09.960
"["The Little Mermaid"] makes it pretty close to&nbsp;
being the best live action Disney movie, however&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:15.660
it still struggles in the villain department.&nbsp;
Halle Bailey IS Ariel and I had literal chills&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:20.709
throughout her performance. This is a little&nbsp;
mermaid retelling like you've never seen before."

00:02:20.709 --> 00:02:26.040
These promising reactions should sooth worried&nbsp;
fans who may be apprehensive about the new remake.

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:32.040
Music is, of course, still a major part of this&nbsp;
live-action "The Little Mermaid," and it still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:37.020
grounds Ariel's narrative as she travels on&nbsp;
her journey of self-discovery. Thankfully,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.020 --> 00:02:43.560
the 2023 remake reportedly nails this part of the&nbsp;
film, thanks to the talented cast led by Bailey,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:50.170
one half of the musical duo Chloe x Halle. Kelly&nbsp;
Rowland of Destiny's Child fame posted on Twitter,

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:54.000
"The Little Mermaid is truly&nbsp;
AN EPIC WATCH!!! The music in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:57.120
this movie!! FREAKINGGGGGGGWOWWWWW!! You laugh,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:02.266
you cry, you'll sing along!! I know I'm gonna&nbsp;
be singing these songs for weeks to come!!!!!!"

00:03:02.266 --> 00:03:04.320
Given her girl group bonafides,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:08.100
this is major praise for the music in&nbsp;
Disney's latest live-action remake.

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:13.200
Several early reactions can't say enough good&nbsp;
things about Bailey's performance as Ariel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:16.980
but there's also plenty of love out&nbsp;
there already for the film's villain.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:20.160
Illuminerdi writer Stephanie Ramirez tweeted,

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:25.080
"["The Little Mermaid"] was an&nbsp;
ABSOLUTE gem! Halle Bailey IS Ariel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:31.140
no matter what anyone says. She brings in the&nbsp;
charm and personality of Ariel to life. Melissa&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:37.462
McCarthy as Ursula was just *chef kiss*.&nbsp;
This film was such a joy to experience."

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:42.300
This was echoed by Fandango writer&nbsp;
Erik Davis, who posted that he also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:46.620
got chills from Bailey's performance,&nbsp;
and labeled McCarthy a "scene stealer."

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:49.260
It seems like "The Little Mermaid" will make a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:52.500
sizable splash when it swims&nbsp;
into theaters on May 24th.

